{"id":8993618,"docketId":66259834,"caseName":"Slayton v. Hammer","caseNameFull":"Slayton, Penitentiary Superintendent v. Hammer Neil, Warden v. Pendergrass Cowan, Penitentiary Superintendent v. Bruce Rose, Warden v. Rivera","slug":"slayton-v-hammer","docketNumber":"No. 71-1245; No. 71-1472; No. 71-1495; No. 72-400","dateFiled":"1973-06-11","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1973,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"Judgments, Would","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8985867,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1290,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"ACm\">C. A. 4th Cir.;</p>\n<p id=\"AdqD\">C. A. 6th Cir. Reported below: <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"301926\"><a href=\"/opinion/301926/martin-v-pendergrass-v-w-s-neil-warden-helen-jones-recor-v-martha-k/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Martin v. Pendergrass v. W. S. Neil, Warden, Helen Jones...\">456 F. 2d 469</a></span> ;</p>\n<p id=\"AE7T\">C. A. 6th Cir. Reported below: <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"302361\"><a href=\"/opinion/302361/william-jacob-bruce-v-john-w-wingo-warden-kentucky-state-penitentiary/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: William Jacob Bruce v. John W. Wingo, Warden, Kentucky...\">457 F. 2d 365</a></span>; and</p>\n<p id=\"AlJC\">C. A. 6th Cir. Reported below: <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"305209\"><a href=\"/opinion/305209/robert-rivera-v-jimmy-rose-warden/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Robert Rivera v. Jimmy Rose, Warden\">465 F. 2d 727</a></span>. Motions of respondents for leave to- proceed <em>in forma pauperis </em>and certiorari granted. Judgments vacated and cases remanded for further consideration in light of <em>Michigan </em>v. <em>Payne, ante, </em>p. 47, and <em>Chaffin </em>v. <em>Stynchcombe, ante, </em>p. 17.</p>\n<judges id=\"AiC\">Mr. Justice Douglas would affirm the judgments.</judges>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}